  <revision rev="26" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>870c969a0c508feea83210f0ca1e49d7</srcmd5>
    <version>2.0.2</version>
    <time>1780426977</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Update to version 2.0.2:
  + This release fixes the following bugs:
    - The Copy button in the Copy File dialog wasn’t set as the
      default action
    - Glitches displaying free space of the current volume
    - Double-clicking tab area created a new tab but didn’t keep
      the selected file
    - Switching tabs didn’t reset Quick Filter
    - Incorrect logic determining when directory monitoring should
      be stopped

- Update to version 2.0.1:
  + This release fixes the following bugs:
    - Right panel would occasionally occupy all available space on
      startup, rendering left panel invisible
    - Color themes were broken with older Gtk versions
    - With older Gtk versions clicking a device button only worked
      once
    - No Quit menu item in the File menu
    - Running search for the first time would list home directory
      contents as “search results”
    - Internal viewer doesn’t allow selecting the first character
      in a line
    - Moving mouse pointer out of the internal viewer window
      selects everything to the start of the visible area

- Update to version 2.0.0:
  + Added embedded terminal to display output of commands run by
    Gnome Commander. The new “Hide Command Line Output When
    Inactive” in “View” menu hides the terminal automatically when</comment>
    <requestid>1356762</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="27" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>1d0fb9d4769652e8bcba316cf5dfe1ce</srcmd5>
    <version>2.0.3</version>
    <time>1781706470</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Update to version 2.0.3:
  + This release fixes the following bugs:
    - JPEG images marked as rotated in metadata weren’t displayed
      rotated
    - Search dialog: “Case sensitive” button for content search had
      reversed effect
    - Size of the Search dialog wasn’t restored after restarting
      application
    - Bogus keyboard input focus after clicking toolbar buttons
    - File list theme wasn’t applied in the Search dialog
    - Overlong contents in file list cells were cut off, not
      ellipsized
    - Internal viewer: incorrect handling of the file start when
      searching for a single character backwards</comment>
    <requestid>1360020</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="28" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>a4ec832f0960eb234ad9c64933be238b</srcmd5>
    <version>2.2.3+5</version>
    <time>1795619672</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Update to version 2.2.3+5:
  * This release includes the following features and changes:
  * New plugin interface:
    + The interface is documented.
    + New built-in plugins have similar but not identical functionality to the
      old ones.
    + Built-in plugins are enabled automatically, user-installed plugins in
      ~/.config/gnome-commander/plugins have to be enabled.
    + Plugins can be written in any programming language.
    + Python-based plugins can import plugin_helper module that makes
      implementation simpler.
    + Context menu scripts are a plugin now. Also, new special comment
      #single-file:true indicates that the script should always be run for each
      file separately.
    + Main menu actions of plugins can be assigned a keyboard shortcut via
      Keyboard Shortcuts dialog.
    + Placing the mouse pointer above the file name in Plugins dialog will show
      the full path to the plugin.
  * Various improvements to the internal viewer:
    + Made all files show up as different tabs within a single viewer window
    + Made case-insensitive search work with non-ASCII letters
    + Remember window’s maximized state (AndriiC)
    + Scroll automatically during selection if the mouse cursor moves out of
      the text
    + Search defaults to the selected text
    + Handle selection via double-click (word) or tripple-click (line)
    + Search only continues from the selection if that selection is visible
    + Improved guessing of preferable display mode when file is opened
    + Implemented extending selection via Shift+Click
    + Implemented extending selection via keyboard (e.g. Shift+Left or
      Shift+Page Down)
    + Pressing Escape will close the search bar even if it isn’t focused.
    + Added support for Ctrl+Left and Ctrl+Right keyboard shortcuts for faster
      horizontal navigation
    + Line length in unwrapped Text mode has been restricted to 4096 characters
      to improve performance
    + Made newline characters visible when they are selected
    + Roughly factor 10 search performance improvement
    + When opening viewer from the Search dialog, the search match is
      immediately selected
    + Fixed handling of newlines in Text mode with CP437 encoding
  * Improvements to handling of removable devices:
    + Eject devices when possible instead of merely unmounting them
    + Fixed recognizing device removal
    + Added support for MTP devices like smartphones
    + Made sure selected connection reflects navigation in and out of a device
      mount directory
  * Other features and changes:
    + Portable builds
    + Added new “Copy File Paths” and “Copy File URIs” actions, their keyboard
      shortcuts can now be configured separately from “Copy File Names”.
    + Improved file column management, allowing to reset column widths and
      apply current settings to all tabs
    + File icon size is set automatically according to font size, the unused
      icon size and scale quality settings have been removed.
    + Keep selected file on directory reload
    + Made navigating back to a directory and switching to a different
      directory then produce the expected navigation history
    + Quick Search is closed when current directory changes
    + When “Rename” action is chosen on file name conflict, renaming keeps file
      extension now
    + Keyboard shortcuts can now be assigned to bookmarks via Keyboard
      Shortcuts dialog.
    + Made displaying directory changes (files added, removed, renamed) more
      consistent and a whole lot faster
    + Open new file list tabs next to the current tab
    + Renaming files will now offer the usual actions if this name already
      exists. Renaming files into a different directory is possible as well.
    + Display a message when a command running in embedded terminal is done
    + Made screen readers say whether a file is selected
    + Added configurable Ctrl+Shift+F10 and Ctrl+Menu keyboard shortcuts to
      open file list header pop-up. Made Shift+F10 and Menu keyboard shortcuts
      configurable as well.
    + Copy File in Current Directory action will now select the new file
    + Improved interoperability of Drag &amp; Drop with other applications
    + Starting Quick Search via non-ASCII letters is possible now.
    + Pressing Escape will close Quick Search even if it isn’t focused.
    + Special file permissions like suid are now displayed in all the relevant
      places, they are left unchanged when file permissions are modified
    + Made Search dialog’s content search work without reading entire files
      into memory
    + When main menu isn’t visible its contents are accessible via a button in
      the title bar
    + Started migrating the code to a new component framework to improve
      maintainability and reliability
    + Added hex search to Search dialog’s content search
    + Listing a large directory no longer hangs Gnome Commander and can now be
      aborted
    + Temporary network connections now show up in all device lists as long as
      they are open.
    + Added keyboard mnemonics to some main menu items that didn’t have any.
  * This release fixes the following bugs:
    + Allowed cancelling file transfers in the middle of a file
    + Spell “KiB” correctly
    + Only reload the destination of copy/move operation if it is a remote
      directory
    + Made file context menu in Advanced Rename dialog apply to the file being
      right-clicked
    + Made Ctrl+Tab/Ctrl+Shift+Tab switch tabs in File Properties dialog
    + Fixed inconsistent updates when multiple directories are removed
    + Made sure clicking device buttons doesn’t leave input focus there
    + Made sure middle-clicking .. opens a new tab (regression in Gnome
      Commander 2.0)
    + Made closing duplicate tabs not leave unnecessary duplicates of locked
      tabs around
    + Cd command on a locked tab was affecting current tab instead of opening a
      new one
    + Running cd dir on command line will no longer change input focus
    + Navigation to a bookmark with a quoted name like 'test' was failing
    + Removed “case-sensitive sorting” option which wasn’t really working
    + Made sure the Bookmarks submenu of the main menu updates on connection or
      bookmark changes
    + Made file icon update when the file changes
    + Do not attempt to calculate size of .. directory
    + Pressing Enter on a file will no longer run command line, only when
      command line is focused
    + Fixed display of selected item in the search results list
    + Fixed embedded terminal actions (Copy/Paste/Select All)
    + Command line history wouldn’t open if some commands are very long
    + Do not allow renaming ..
    + Pressing Delete in a text field in the Search dialog no longer suggests
      deleting a file
    + Fixed crash when copying files to a read-only file system and choosing
      “Replace All”
    + Fixed input focus issues when closing a submenu of the file context menu
    + Changes to format options apply immediately now
    + Fixed internal viewer displaying and copying newlines as dots in ASCII
      mode
    + Do not display file permissions for ..
    + Display file’s context menu when right-clicking its icon
    + Moving up in internal viewer while in wrapped text mode wouldn’t reach
      start of file
    + Corrected mouse selection in internal viewer’s Fixed Width mode when tab
      characters are present
    + Display selected tab characters with correct width in internal viewer’s
      Text mode
    + Made search result selection in internal viewer work with invalid UTF-8
      correctly
    + Resolved keyboard mnemonics conflict in the File menu between “Search”
      and “Create Symbolic Link”
    + New or updated docs: hu (Balázs Úr), kk (Baurzhan Muftakhidinov), ru
      (Sergej A.), sv
  * Updated translations.
- Disable update of vendored dependencies, it currently breaks the build if we
  do.</comment>
    <requestid>1400551</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
